---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Phalita">
  <header class="masthead">
    <p class="kicker">फल · phalita</p>
    <h1>A reading of the birth chart</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      Drawn from Phaladīpikā, verse by verse. Every statement is a condition the
      text states, tested against the chart — and where the text argues with
      itself, both sides are shown.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="chapter">
    <div class="body">
      <p>
        Birth data goes in; the reading comes out. Ten chapters on the sectors of
        life — work, money, marriage, children, home, body, mind, fortune, family,
        dharma — followed by the verses behind them and a catalogue of 250
        questions.
      </p>
      <p>
        No death date is produced. A grave reading is never pronounced from a
        single condition: Phaladīpikā 15.6 requires two to agree, and where they
        do not, the engine withholds rather than guesses.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p style="margin-top:2.5rem"><a href="./reading" style="color:var(--accent)">Read a chart →</a></p>
</Base>
